# The DS5500's SCSI software, run 1 of 3: /sau14/scsi14.drvr from
# 019594-002 file 3. The volume tools/dn5500/restore.script produces has none of
# the four pieces a SCSI round trip needs; these three runs restore them object
# by object with the volume's own /install/tools/rbak_sr10, rather than a whole
# MINST pass. One object per run keeps each run short enough to end cleanly,
# which --disk-writeback and the report both need. README.md has the invocation.
#
# rbak's own help: `{-pn|-all} [-as disk_pn]`, pathnames not wildcards. `$ `
# anchors, never two identical expects in a row; EOT then `shut` at the `)`
# prompt commits the single-level store (FINDINGS.md C196).
expect MD14
expect >
send DI W\r
expect >
send EX DOMAIN_OS\r
expect )
send SH\r
expect login:
send user\r
expect Password
send \r
expect $
send /install/tools/rbak_sr10 -dev ct -f 3 install/ri.apollo.os.v.10.4/sau14/scsi14.drvr -as /sau14/scsi14.drvr\r
expect Restore complete
send ld /sau14\r
expect $
send \x04
expect Returned status
expect : ok
expect )
send shut\r
expect Shutdown successful
